./logs/iter_001_idea_01_explorer_01.stdout.log:48:The \(\beta\)-calculation is sound because the definition takes \(\sup_a\), and \(a=0\) is allowed. Conditioning on \(P_1,\dots,P_{s_n}\) does not reveal \(U_{n+1}\), but \(U_{n+1}>0\) almost surely, so the next positive price occurs exactly at \(s_{n+1}\).
./logs/iter_001_idea_01_explorer_01.stdout.log:50:The comparator bound is also sound. The solver’s argument uses only the maximum possible spike height, not the exact trade probability, so it is a valid upper bound. It correctly handles the fact that a quote posted at \(t=s_{m^*}\) cannot trade on the current spike, only on future prices.
./logs/iter_001_idea_01_explorer_01.stdout.log:52:The continuum-max issue is not a gap in this construction because the spike heights have continuous distributions and only finitely many spikes appear before any fixed horizon.
